1
00:00:01,068 --> 00:00:02,092
<i>Previously on</i> Gotham...

2
00:00:02,169 --> 00:00:03,535
You're the brother I never had.

3
00:00:03,670 --> 00:00:05,696
We will create a
legacy in this city.

4
00:00:06,039 --> 00:00:07,234
<i>Gotham falls,</i>

5
00:00:07,541 --> 00:00:08,541
<i>we rise.</i>

6
00:00:09,109 --> 00:00:10,109
Together.

7
00:00:10,310 --> 00:00:11,369
BARBARA: <i>Poor Jim.</i>

8
00:00:11,512 --> 00:00:12,512
All alone again.

9
00:00:12,579 --> 00:00:14,605
- I told you to leave.
- I heard you.

10
00:00:15,349 --> 00:00:17,109
GORDON: <i>So many
things I wish I could change.</i>

11
00:00:17,217 --> 00:00:18,241
Things I've done.

12
00:00:18,385 --> 00:00:20,251
We're here now. We'll try to put

13
00:00:20,387 --> 00:00:21,685
the pieces back together again.

14
00:00:22,055 --> 00:00:22,579
BARBARA: <i>Jim,</i>

15
00:00:22,723 --> 00:00:23,723
I'm pregnant.

16
00:00:24,791 --> 00:00:27,317
- This isn't you.
- We're not the same.

17
00:00:27,461 --> 00:00:29,487
<i>That night that your
parents were murdered,</i>

18
00:00:29,796 --> 00:00:32,698
<i>I didn't do anything,
because I didn't care.</i>

19
00:00:33,033 --> 00:00:35,434
Everyone, let's
dig a little deeper.

20
00:00:35,636 --> 00:00:37,764
'Cause that's the only
way you're all making it out

21
00:00:38,105 --> 00:00:39,105
of this hole.

22
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:41,770
- SELINA:
Deep enough?
- (groans)

23
00:00:42,142 --> 00:00:43,371
You're leaving Gotham.

24
00:00:43,510 --> 00:00:45,430
OSWALD: <i>There's nothing
left for me here anymore.</i>

25
00:00:45,479 --> 00:00:46,538
<i>I've done all I can.</i>

26
00:00:46,680 --> 00:00:47,680
I want in.

27
00:00:49,116 --> 00:00:49,674
(grunting)

28
00:00:49,816 --> 00:00:53,150
JEREMIAH: <i>I love
family reunions.</i>

29
00:00:53,420 --> 00:00:54,444
Don't you?

30
00:00:59,593 --> 00:01:02,256
(grunting)

31
00:01:02,462 --> 00:01:03,725
Go. Go, go.

32
00:01:04,798 --> 00:01:06,460
(indistinct shouting)

33
00:01:08,168 --> 00:01:10,137
♪♪

34
00:01:17,744 --> 00:01:19,212
- Which way?
- Wait.

35
00:01:19,680 --> 00:01:21,444
♪♪

36
00:01:25,719 --> 00:01:27,187
(whizzing)

37
00:01:32,626 --> 00:01:35,391
(coughing)

38
00:01:39,166 --> 00:01:41,397
(choking)

39
00:01:43,837 --> 00:01:45,806
♪♪

40
00:01:50,744 --> 00:01:51,744
General,

41
00:01:52,145 --> 00:01:53,705
you were the ones
who let Walker operate

42
00:01:53,847 --> 00:01:55,281
right under your noses.

43
00:01:55,782 --> 00:01:57,580
Now you're telling me
she evaded capture?

44
00:01:57,818 --> 00:01:59,514
WADE: I understand
your frustration.

45
00:01:59,886 --> 00:02:02,253
Have you at least determined
why she did what she did?

46
00:02:02,756 --> 00:02:03,756
Not yet.

47
00:02:04,224 --> 00:02:05,590
Look, bottom line,

48
00:02:06,226 --> 00:02:08,195
Walker and Dorrance
are out of the picture.

49
00:02:08,395 --> 00:02:10,489
What else is standing in
the way of reunification?

50
00:02:10,631 --> 00:02:11,631
WADE: Nothing.

51
00:02:11,698 --> 00:02:14,258
I'm recommending we begin
the process immediately.

52
00:02:14,768 --> 00:02:17,431
There have been a lot of
promises from across the river.

53
00:02:17,604 --> 00:02:19,664
WADE: But unlike
Walker, or whoever she is,

54
00:02:19,806 --> 00:02:21,604
I have the authority
to take action.

55
00:02:21,742 --> 00:02:24,610
Unless something happens
to destabilize Gotham again,

56
00:02:24,745 --> 00:02:26,611
this nightmare is about to end.

57
00:02:27,514 --> 00:02:28,674
BULLOCK: <i>Think he's for real?</i>

58
00:02:28,749 --> 00:02:30,240
I'll believe it when it happens.

59
00:02:30,384 --> 00:02:32,353
I take it your search
party didn't find Alfred.

60
00:02:32,519 --> 00:02:33,680
Neither hide nor hair.

61
00:02:34,621 --> 00:02:36,146
Pennyworth vanished
five days ago.

62
00:02:36,289 --> 00:02:37,289
It ain't looking good.

63
00:02:37,557 --> 00:02:38,557
How's Bruce?

64
00:02:39,326 --> 00:02:41,625
He's been pulling double
shifts on the search parties.

65
00:02:42,262 --> 00:02:43,787
Kid's dead on his feet.

66
00:02:49,369 --> 00:02:50,613
I want to search this area next.

67
00:02:50,637 --> 00:02:52,148
There are whole blocks
of abandoned buildings.

68
00:02:52,172 --> 00:02:53,783
- I'll get a squad right on it.
- Just give me five minutes.

69
00:02:53,807 --> 00:02:55,241
- I'll be ready.
- No.

70
00:02:55,575 --> 00:02:56,440
You're not going out.

71
00:02:56,576 --> 00:02:58,306
- No, Jim...
- You need your rest.

72
00:02:58,445 --> 00:03:00,245
I'm not cutting you out,
but I need you sharp,

73
00:03:00,313 --> 00:03:01,508
not a liability.

74
00:03:05,952 --> 00:03:08,217
I just don't understand
what could have happened.

75
00:03:08,455 --> 00:03:09,479
Neither do I.

76
00:03:10,457 --> 00:03:11,534
But I know that
Alfred Pennyworth

77
00:03:11,558 --> 00:03:12,821
can take care of himself.

78
00:03:14,628 --> 00:03:16,221
I'll send for you
if I hear anything.

79
00:03:24,204 --> 00:03:24,762
Kid's tough.

80
00:03:24,905 --> 00:03:25,905
Yeah.

81
00:03:26,373 --> 00:03:28,205
In other good-ish
news, Harper radioed.

82
00:03:28,341 --> 00:03:29,400
Her squad found something.

83
00:03:29,776 --> 00:03:30,776
What?

84
00:03:32,412 --> 00:03:33,436
It's weird.

85
00:03:34,247 --> 00:03:35,887
- (camera shutter clicks)
- (siren whoops)

86
00:03:35,949 --> 00:03:36,949
HARPER: Four men.

87
00:03:37,951 --> 00:03:39,762
Looks like they breathed in
some sort of chemical agent.

88
00:03:39,786 --> 00:03:40,879
I'm thinking airborne.

89
00:03:41,621 --> 00:03:42,953
And the Z's on their bodies?

90
00:03:43,457 --> 00:03:44,937
Carved into them
before time of death.

91
00:03:45,425 --> 00:03:46,654
Check out the mustache.

92
00:03:50,597 --> 00:03:51,929
- Fake.
- Seems like

93
00:03:52,265 --> 00:03:53,699
they escaped from here.

94
00:03:56,670 --> 00:03:57,729
GORDON: A film set?

95
00:03:57,938 --> 00:03:59,236
HARPER: I said it was weird.

96
00:04:00,307 --> 00:04:01,832
BULLOCK: Zs on their chests.

97
00:04:02,542 --> 00:04:03,976
Think it could be Zsasz?

98
00:04:05,445 --> 00:04:06,936
Chemicals aren't really his MO.

99
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:09,647
Plus, I never figured Zsasz
for much of a cinephile.

100
00:04:10,383 --> 00:04:12,495
But whoever it is, if they
have more of these chemicals

101
00:04:12,519 --> 00:04:13,599
and the will to use them...

102
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:15,313
It's bye-bye, reunification.

103
00:04:16,256 --> 00:04:18,885
Got to stop him before
news reaches the mainland.

104
00:04:20,994 --> 00:04:21,994
The Chessmen.

105
00:04:22,929 --> 00:04:24,169
That's a gang that operates out

106
00:04:24,264 --> 00:04:25,708
of the Narrows. What
the hell is a Narrows gang

107
00:04:25,732 --> 00:04:26,825
doing way up here?

108
00:04:26,967 --> 00:04:29,630
I think we both know
someone we can ask.

109
00:04:34,307 --> 00:04:36,003
♪♪

110
00:04:52,025 --> 00:04:53,926
♪♪

111
00:05:13,847 --> 00:05:14,847
(woman laughs)

112
00:05:26,326 --> 00:05:28,022
♪♪

113
00:05:58,792 --> 00:06:00,693
♪♪

114
00:06:22,082 --> 00:06:24,381
(indistinct chatter)

115
00:06:24,517 --> 00:06:25,862
Can you check on
the fever in Bed 12?

116
00:06:25,886 --> 00:06:26,979
What's up, Doc?

117
00:06:27,554 --> 00:06:29,523
Heard you were
working here. Interesting.

118
00:06:29,656 --> 00:06:30,988
It's what I do, help people.

119
00:06:31,124 --> 00:06:33,491
Speaking of which,
I've got patients.

120
00:06:33,627 --> 00:06:35,926
Oh, you wouldn't kick
Jim's baby mama to the curb,

121
00:06:36,062 --> 00:06:38,156
- now, would you?
- Whatever happened
between you

122
00:06:38,498 --> 00:06:39,966
and Jim, it's none
of my concern.

123
00:06:40,100 --> 00:06:41,143
So if you're here to gloat...

124
00:06:41,167 --> 00:06:42,760
I'm here for medical assistance.

125
00:06:43,637 --> 00:06:44,798
For my little nugget.

126
00:06:45,639 --> 00:06:46,639
What do you say?

127
00:06:46,706 --> 00:06:47,435
Be my O.B.?

128
00:06:47,574 --> 00:06:48,735
You can't be serious.

129
00:06:48,875 --> 00:06:50,434
I know we've had
our differences.

130
00:06:50,577 --> 00:06:52,136
You tried to kill me, Barbara.

131
00:06:52,612 --> 00:06:53,612
Twice.

132
00:06:54,114 --> 00:06:55,844
That was years ago.

133
00:06:55,982 --> 00:06:57,177
There are other doctors here.

134
00:06:57,584 --> 00:06:58,745
Not as good as you.

135
00:06:59,185 --> 00:07:00,185
Look,

136
00:07:00,487 --> 00:07:01,853
whatever you
think of me, my child

137
00:07:01,988 --> 00:07:03,684
is innocent, and I
want the best for it.

138
00:07:03,890 --> 00:07:05,654
And in this place,
that means you.

139
00:07:07,961 --> 00:07:09,020
(sighs)

140
00:07:09,562 --> 00:07:10,602
Does Jim know you're here?

141
00:07:10,697 --> 00:07:12,457
- This is none
of his business.
- (door opens)

142
00:07:12,599 --> 00:07:13,599
GORDON: Lee?

143
00:07:17,037 --> 00:07:18,037
Jim.

144
00:07:20,173 --> 00:07:21,937
- Barbara.
- BARBARA:
You're interrupting.

145
00:07:22,175 --> 00:07:24,110
Doctor-patient. Blow.

146
00:07:24,511 --> 00:07:25,672
I'm sorry, you're her doctor?

147
00:07:25,812 --> 00:07:26,939
No. I don't know.

148
00:07:27,580 --> 00:07:29,446
Maybe. What are you doing here?

149
00:07:30,583 --> 00:07:31,583
Some bodies turned up.

150
00:07:31,651 --> 00:07:33,091
They might have a
Narrows connection.

151
00:07:33,453 --> 00:07:34,573
I wouldn't have come, but...

152
00:07:34,688 --> 00:07:36,088
It's important. Right.

153
00:07:37,557 --> 00:07:40,493
You two need to
talk. I'll be outside.

154
00:07:40,627 --> 00:07:42,738
- Uh, I'd rather not.
- If you want me
to be your doctor,

155
00:07:42,762 --> 00:07:45,527
you will talk to
the baby's... father.

156
00:07:46,499 --> 00:07:48,577
Your first appointment is next
week. The nurse will give you

157
00:07:48,601 --> 00:07:49,812
all your vitamins
when you leave.

158
00:07:49,836 --> 00:07:50,836
Deal?

159
00:07:59,746 --> 00:08:01,190
Is she really the only
one you could find?

160
00:08:01,214 --> 00:08:03,206
She's the best doctor
in this hellhole of a city.

161
00:08:03,583 --> 00:08:04,894
Not everything is
about Jim Gordon.

162
00:08:04,918 --> 00:08:05,918
Pretty sure this one is.

163
00:08:06,052 --> 00:08:07,714
Because we slept together. Yeah.

164
00:08:08,488 --> 00:08:10,599
I only told you because I
felt you had a right to know.

165
00:08:10,623 --> 00:08:12,023
But your involvement
in this ended

166
00:08:12,158 --> 00:08:13,990
the moment you put
your pants back on.

167
00:08:14,194 --> 00:08:15,628
(scoffs)

168
00:08:17,931 --> 00:08:18,955
What?

169
00:08:20,233 --> 00:08:21,577
You don't think I'm
fit to be a mother?

170
00:08:21,601 --> 00:08:22,660
What do you think?

171
00:08:25,572 --> 00:08:26,631
Barbara.

172
00:08:30,944 --> 00:08:32,537
(door opens forcefully)

173
00:08:32,746 --> 00:08:34,544
(rats squeaking)

174
00:08:50,897 --> 00:08:52,832
(woman laughing)

175
00:09:01,841 --> 00:09:04,037
(clinking)

176
00:09:04,177 --> 00:09:06,043
(laughing continues)

177
00:09:15,889 --> 00:09:17,858
(speaks inaudibly)

178
00:09:17,991 --> 00:09:20,153
(giggles)

179
00:09:23,930 --> 00:09:25,159
Who are you?

180
00:09:26,733 --> 00:09:28,326
Well, look who
decided to join us.

181
00:09:28,701 --> 00:09:29,725
Hello, champ.

182
00:09:33,940 --> 00:09:35,067
ALFRED: Master Bruce!

183
00:09:35,575 --> 00:09:36,668
Alfred, how did you...

184
00:09:36,910 --> 00:09:38,139
Look at the state of you.

185
00:09:38,578 --> 00:09:40,698
What have I told you about
rolling around in the muck?

186
00:09:41,981 --> 00:09:44,007
Alfred, what's going on?

187
00:09:44,150 --> 00:09:45,150
Who are these people?

188
00:09:45,185 --> 00:09:46,710
MAN: Whatever do
you mean, Bruce?

189
00:09:47,954 --> 00:09:49,217
We're your parents.

190
00:09:51,191 --> 00:09:52,784
Right. Well, let's
get you spruced up.

191
00:09:53,326 --> 00:09:54,326
After all,

192
00:09:55,061 --> 00:09:56,256
we have a guest.

193
00:10:00,066 --> 00:10:02,228
Welcome home, Bruce.

194
00:10:07,207 --> 00:10:10,234
Jeremiah. You're alive.

195
00:10:10,376 --> 00:10:14,814
(laughs) Well, you
didn't think Selina

196
00:10:14,948 --> 00:10:16,814
could kill me so
easily, did you?

197
00:10:17,016 --> 00:10:20,282
(laughs) I just had to
put you off my scent

198
00:10:20,620 --> 00:10:23,283
until I could
finalize my... project.

199
00:10:23,990 --> 00:10:25,652
Manners, Master Bruce.

200
00:10:26,059 --> 00:10:27,299
Let's not be rude to our guest.

201
00:10:27,360 --> 00:10:29,886
Especially when I
come bearing gifts.

202
00:10:30,964 --> 00:10:33,195
ALFRED: Oh,
Mr. Jeremiah. A cake.

203
00:10:33,700 --> 00:10:35,032
How exceedingly kind of you.

204
00:10:35,935 --> 00:10:37,130
Is it Italian meringue?

205
00:10:38,204 --> 00:10:39,204
Sure.

206
00:10:39,272 --> 00:10:40,272
Oh.

207
00:10:40,740 --> 00:10:42,140
Now, now, Bruce, you come

208
00:10:42,275 --> 00:10:44,210
any closer and I
blow up Wayne Manor,

209
00:10:44,344 --> 00:10:45,835
with all of us inside of it.

210
00:10:45,979 --> 00:10:47,948
I have a dozen
more of these, uh,

211
00:10:48,281 --> 00:10:52,013
Italian meringues sprinkled
all throughout the house.

212
00:10:53,086 --> 00:10:54,816
What did you do to Alfred?

213
00:10:55,655 --> 00:10:56,918
And who are these people?

214
00:10:57,056 --> 00:10:58,217
Ah, glad you asked.

215
00:10:58,358 --> 00:10:59,358
Mm, come.

216
00:10:59,792 --> 00:11:00,816
(quietly): Come, come.

217
00:11:02,729 --> 00:11:05,062
JEREMIAH: Mommy
and Daddy dearest

218
00:11:05,732 --> 00:11:09,191
were just an innocent
couple I kidnapped based on...

219
00:11:09,802 --> 00:11:12,101
bone structure and, um...

220
00:11:13,406 --> 00:11:14,406
build.

221
00:11:15,208 --> 00:11:16,403
Just a touch

222
00:11:16,743 --> 00:11:19,338
of plastic surgery, and voilà...

223
00:11:20,713 --> 00:11:21,713
Waynes.

224
00:11:21,881 --> 00:11:23,076
(chuckles)

225
00:11:23,249 --> 00:11:25,275
Alfred I nabbed
in the Green Zone.

226
00:11:25,985 --> 00:11:27,317
They're hypnotized.

227
00:11:27,453 --> 00:11:29,081
Well, I'm afraid
there was no room

228
00:11:29,222 --> 00:11:30,781
for improv in our script.

229
00:11:30,990 --> 00:11:32,322
Today is a...

230
00:11:32,759 --> 00:11:35,092
<i>very</i> important day, Bruce.

231
00:11:36,996 --> 00:11:39,431
Just look at the
way they're dressed.

232
00:11:42,202 --> 00:11:44,068
It's the night my
parents were killed.

233
00:11:45,004 --> 00:11:46,233
And I'm giving you the chance

234
00:11:46,372 --> 00:11:49,342
to experience it all over again.

235
00:11:51,377 --> 00:11:52,377
Why?

236
00:11:53,012 --> 00:11:54,378
Isn't it obvious?

237
00:11:57,984 --> 00:11:59,008
Bruce...

238
00:12:00,453 --> 00:12:01,477
this...

239
00:12:01,955 --> 00:12:05,255
this was the most
important day of your life.

240
00:12:07,427 --> 00:12:09,919
And I didn't get
to be a part of it.

241
00:12:11,998 --> 00:12:13,762
We need to rectify that.

242
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:16,162
Alfred. It's time for dinner.

243
00:12:16,936 --> 00:12:19,735
Chop-chop. We're on
a very tight schedule.

244
00:12:19,939 --> 00:12:21,931
Of course, Mr. Jeremiah.

245
00:12:24,510 --> 00:12:26,775
(motor chugging)

246
00:12:37,757 --> 00:12:40,750
(explosion)

247
00:12:40,893 --> 00:12:42,759
That's zero for three.

248
00:12:43,997 --> 00:12:44,997
Yes.

249
00:12:45,198 --> 00:12:46,838
It seems the government
was quite thorough

250
00:12:46,966 --> 00:12:49,060
- when they mined
the river.
- You didn't have a plan

251
00:12:49,202 --> 00:12:52,001
to get off this rock <i>before</i>
you stole everyone's crap?

252
00:12:52,405 --> 00:12:54,931
I was working on a plan.

253
00:12:55,174 --> 00:12:56,904
The river is mined.

254
00:12:57,043 --> 00:12:59,808
Everything that flies out
gets blown from... the...

255
00:12:59,946 --> 00:13:01,847
- sky.
- What?

256
00:13:03,483 --> 00:13:06,544
Jeremiah was digging
a tunnel under the river.

257
00:13:07,854 --> 00:13:08,854
A tunnel?

258
00:13:09,055 --> 00:13:10,853
(chuckles) Really?

259
00:13:11,124 --> 00:13:13,252
Do you have any better ideas?

260
00:13:17,196 --> 00:13:18,562
Didn't think so.

261
00:13:19,866 --> 00:13:21,027
It's in the Dark Zone.

262
00:13:21,501 --> 00:13:23,231
We should wait until
night to check it out.

263
00:13:23,436 --> 00:13:26,235
Well, I was running out
of guinea pigs anyway.

264
00:13:29,175 --> 00:13:30,175
Oh, look!

265
00:13:30,276 --> 00:13:31,437
He's swimming to shore.

266
00:13:31,878 --> 00:13:33,346
(explosion)

267
00:13:39,218 --> 00:13:39,981
THOMPKINS: <i>Are you sure</i>

268
00:13:40,119 --> 00:13:41,917
you should be out
in the Narrows alone?

269
00:13:42,055 --> 00:13:44,286
When the bridges fell, this
place descended into chaos.

270
00:13:44,424 --> 00:13:46,368
Figure our best bet of
getting out in one piece is

271
00:13:46,392 --> 00:13:49,271
- to keep a low profile.
- So all the work I did
to make the Narrows better

272
00:13:49,295 --> 00:13:50,888
- was for nothing.
- (loud clattering)

273
00:13:51,030 --> 00:13:52,362
(indistinct shouts,
man whistles)

274
00:13:52,498 --> 00:13:54,524
It's the Leopards.
Rivals of the Chessmen.

275
00:13:57,170 --> 00:13:58,604
(men speaking indistinctly)

276
00:14:00,273 --> 00:14:01,104
About this Barbara thing...

277
00:14:01,240 --> 00:14:02,333
Uh, Jim, just don't.

278
00:14:02,475 --> 00:14:04,842
No, it's important to
me that you understand.

279
00:14:05,878 --> 00:14:07,107
(sighs)

280
00:14:07,380 --> 00:14:09,508
Okay. So, what are you gonna do?

281
00:14:12,618 --> 00:14:14,587
I don't know, but
it's my child, too.

282
00:14:17,256 --> 00:14:19,384
Barbara seems to have
a difference of opinion.

283
00:14:20,293 --> 00:14:21,352
But hey, people change.

284
00:14:22,161 --> 00:14:23,321
You don't know her like I do.

285
00:14:23,396 --> 00:14:24,455
You can say that again.

286
00:14:24,597 --> 00:14:27,192
(engine revs, pulls away)

287
00:14:27,333 --> 00:14:28,333
Look.

288
00:14:30,503 --> 00:14:31,503
We're clear.

289
00:14:32,605 --> 00:14:34,164
The Chessmen moved around.

290
00:14:34,307 --> 00:14:36,071
They used these as
signals for their members.

291
00:14:36,542 --> 00:14:37,662
The rook's a compass needle.

292
00:14:38,077 --> 00:14:39,602
North-northeast. Let's go.

293
00:14:39,946 --> 00:14:41,642
♪♪

294
00:14:54,627 --> 00:14:55,627
Hmm.

295
00:14:56,396 --> 00:14:58,661
Alfred told me
such great tidbits

296
00:14:58,998 --> 00:15:00,227
about your childhood.

297
00:15:00,666 --> 00:15:02,532
How you used to eat here,

298
00:15:02,935 --> 00:15:05,495
in the kitchen, when it
was just you and the family.

299
00:15:06,005 --> 00:15:07,530
My, how...

300
00:15:07,974 --> 00:15:10,170
homey and intimate.

301
00:15:12,445 --> 00:15:16,177
Grilled cheese and Branston
pickle sandwich, Mr. Jeremiah.

302
00:15:16,315 --> 00:15:17,510
Master Bruce's favorite.

303
00:15:17,984 --> 00:15:21,182
My influence, though
Thomas did add a dash

304
00:15:21,320 --> 00:15:23,414
of aioli for extra flair.

305
00:15:24,557 --> 00:15:27,220
(laughing)

306
00:15:30,096 --> 00:15:31,564
Oh. Come on, Bruce.

307
00:15:31,697 --> 00:15:34,462
That's a weird favorite
food for a 12-year-old.

308
00:15:35,034 --> 00:15:36,502
I'm playing your game.

309
00:15:38,304 --> 00:15:40,102
Now let Alfred and
these people go.

310
00:15:40,239 --> 00:15:41,298
They're innocent.

311
00:15:42,108 --> 00:15:44,043
I'm sorry, Bruce, it's just...

312
00:15:44,444 --> 00:15:46,675
it's very important
to me that I get

313
00:15:47,079 --> 00:15:50,140
every detail exactly right.

314
00:15:50,283 --> 00:15:51,546
Speaking of which...

315
00:15:51,951 --> 00:15:53,351
the final touch.

316
00:15:57,957 --> 00:15:59,653
♪♪

317
00:16:05,431 --> 00:16:07,161
What was it like...

318
00:16:08,234 --> 00:16:10,203
losing your parents that night?

319
00:16:10,470 --> 00:16:11,470
(deep, distorted gunshot)

320
00:16:13,506 --> 00:16:16,374
I lost my family, too, Bruce.

321
00:16:17,643 --> 00:16:19,612
The wound still hasn't healed.

322
00:16:19,745 --> 00:16:22,510
I... think about it often.

323
00:16:23,015 --> 00:16:24,381
None of this is real.

324
00:16:26,986 --> 00:16:29,046
You're trying to manipulate me.

325
00:16:31,524 --> 00:16:33,390
It will never be real.

326
00:16:36,295 --> 00:16:39,527
But you are thinking
about that night.

327
00:16:40,299 --> 00:16:42,097
That's all I need.

328
00:16:43,302 --> 00:16:45,237
I just want to be
connected to you.

329
00:16:45,371 --> 00:16:48,500
I offered for you to
be my best friend!

330
00:16:54,614 --> 00:16:57,049
But I've realized if we...

331
00:16:57,250 --> 00:16:59,515
can't be friends...

332
00:17:00,620 --> 00:17:03,749
then we <i>can</i> be
connected in other ways.

333
00:17:07,360 --> 00:17:08,521
How?

334
00:17:11,163 --> 00:17:12,495
You'll see.

335
00:17:14,400 --> 00:17:15,766
In time.

336
00:17:23,743 --> 00:17:24,743
Hmm.

337
00:17:26,279 --> 00:17:28,544
I'm sorry to cut
tonight short...

338
00:17:29,482 --> 00:17:30,482
but...

339
00:17:31,317 --> 00:17:33,616
your parents and I have
a very important date...

340
00:17:33,753 --> 00:17:34,550
Jeremiah.

341
00:17:34,687 --> 00:17:36,485
- With destiny.
- Jeremiah!

342
00:17:36,689 --> 00:17:40,057
You might want to find
your faithful butler and leave.

343
00:17:40,693 --> 00:17:41,693
Quickly.

344
00:17:41,827 --> 00:17:44,524
(steady beeping)

345
00:17:45,665 --> 00:17:46,665
Alfred!

346
00:17:50,303 --> 00:17:52,204
(bell tolling)

347
00:17:58,144 --> 00:17:59,476
The signs lead this way.

348
00:18:00,513 --> 00:18:01,537
Look at the smoke.

349
00:18:01,781 --> 00:18:03,773
Someone restarted production.

350
00:18:04,850 --> 00:18:09,618
(tanks burbling)

351
00:18:22,768 --> 00:18:24,327
My God, Jim...

352
00:18:25,805 --> 00:18:27,205
look at all of this.

353
00:18:28,207 --> 00:18:29,207
Come on.

354
00:18:35,147 --> 00:18:37,173
- Who's in charge here?
- (softly):
Tick tock,

355
00:18:37,316 --> 00:18:38,316
the chemical stock,

356
00:18:38,384 --> 00:18:40,216
shall give our
Gotham an aftershock.

357
00:18:40,720 --> 00:18:42,348
Tick tock, the chemical stock,

358
00:18:42,622 --> 00:18:44,215
shall give our
Gotham an aftershock.

359
00:18:44,357 --> 00:18:46,326
Tick tock, the chemical stock...

360
00:18:46,459 --> 00:18:48,360
shall give our
Gotham an aftershock.

361
00:18:48,494 --> 00:18:49,553
They've been hypnotized.

362
00:18:50,196 --> 00:18:51,196
Tetch.

363
00:18:51,330 --> 00:18:52,507
- (one person clapping)
- WORKERS:
Tick tock,

364
00:18:52,531 --> 00:18:53,760
the chemical stock

365
00:18:54,367 --> 00:18:56,893
shall give our
Gotham an aftershock.

366
00:18:57,303 --> 00:18:59,499
My, my, what a thrill.

367
00:19:00,272 --> 00:19:01,501
Jim Gordon...

368
00:19:02,541 --> 00:19:03,821
and the woman
he told me to kill.

369
00:19:03,876 --> 00:19:05,777
(mock gasp) Brings
back memories.

370
00:19:06,178 --> 00:19:08,670
That tea party, so long ago.

371
00:19:09,582 --> 00:19:12,313
But now, to order these
men to attack my foe!

372
00:19:12,451 --> 00:19:13,451
(Thompkins yelps)

373
00:19:15,454 --> 00:19:17,184
JERVIS: All for
one, and one for all!

374
00:19:17,323 --> 00:19:19,189
Ain't this a grand old ball!

375
00:19:19,392 --> 00:19:20,392
(grunts)

376
00:19:22,161 --> 00:19:24,392
(pipes clanging)

377
00:19:25,531 --> 00:19:26,531
Yoo-hoo!

378
00:19:26,799 --> 00:19:27,799
(gasps) Jim!

379
00:19:27,867 --> 00:19:29,460
Ain't this...

380
00:19:29,669 --> 00:19:32,662
some... game!

381
00:19:37,243 --> 00:19:38,438
Give it to me again?

382
00:19:39,445 --> 00:19:41,175
(sighs) Penguin
has been stealing

383
00:19:41,313 --> 00:19:43,407
everything in the city
that's not nailed down,

384
00:19:43,582 --> 00:19:45,915
and now he needs a way
of getting it off the island.

385
00:19:46,352 --> 00:19:48,719
Hmm. And you're helping him?

386
00:19:48,954 --> 00:19:50,479
Well, that's what he thinks.

387
00:19:51,691 --> 00:19:53,557
Barbara, Tabitha
was my friend, too.

388
00:19:53,926 --> 00:19:55,724
If anything, I want
to gut the twerp...

389
00:19:56,829 --> 00:19:58,869
- and take his loot.
- Except you don't
actually have

390
00:19:58,931 --> 00:20:01,400
- a way out of Gotham.
- I'll find one tonight.

391
00:20:01,534 --> 00:20:03,435
I'll still need your
help moving the stuff.

392
00:20:03,569 --> 00:20:05,401
We can get out of here together.

393
00:20:07,406 --> 00:20:08,669
Away from Jim Gordon.

394
00:20:09,408 --> 00:20:10,774
Rich as Midas.

395
00:20:10,976 --> 00:20:12,604
Penguin dead in a ditch.

396
00:20:13,679 --> 00:20:15,910
Well, aren't we just two
single ladies and a baby

397
00:20:16,248 --> 00:20:18,547
about to kill our
sworn enemy together.

398
00:20:19,819 --> 00:20:20,819
What?

399
00:20:21,554 --> 00:20:22,886
It's just you're pregnant.

400
00:20:23,355 --> 00:20:24,687
Don't even start.

401
00:20:28,427 --> 00:20:29,547
BRUCE (in distance): Alfred!

402
00:20:29,595 --> 00:20:30,595
(beeping)

403
00:20:31,263 --> 00:20:31,923
(in distance): Alfred!

404
00:20:32,264 --> 00:20:33,459
(running footsteps)

405
00:20:33,632 --> 00:20:36,500
- (beeping)
- Alfred. We need
to get out of here.

406
00:20:36,635 --> 00:20:38,595
Ah, Master Bruce. I was
just taking a quiet moment

407
00:20:38,637 --> 00:20:39,969
- to tidy up.
- We need to go.

408
00:20:40,406 --> 00:20:42,238
- The bombs.
- What bombs?

409
00:20:42,608 --> 00:20:43,701
These bombs.

410
00:20:45,578 --> 00:20:46,778
No need for roughhousing, sir.

411
00:20:46,912 --> 00:20:49,313
(beeping continues)

412
00:20:49,782 --> 00:20:51,250
There has to be a way.

413
00:20:52,551 --> 00:20:53,962
Alfred, you'd do anything
to protect me, right?

414
00:20:53,986 --> 00:20:56,956
- Absolutely, sir.
- There's a gas leak. In the kitchen.

415
00:20:57,289 --> 00:20:59,434
It's only a matter of time
before this whole place goes up.

416
00:20:59,458 --> 00:21:01,359
A gas leak? Where
are your parents?

417
00:21:01,494 --> 00:21:03,305
- Where's our guest?
- I've already warned them.

418
00:21:03,329 --> 00:21:04,558
I know a way out. Come on!

419
00:21:05,664 --> 00:21:08,691
(rapid beeping)

420
00:21:10,936 --> 00:21:12,905
(deep rumbling)

421
00:21:35,361 --> 00:21:36,454
BRUCE: Alfred!

422
00:21:37,897 --> 00:21:38,897
Alfred.

423
00:21:39,031 --> 00:21:40,031
(groans)

424
00:21:40,833 --> 00:21:41,833
(groans)

425
00:21:42,034 --> 00:21:43,297
Oh, bloody hell.

426
00:21:43,569 --> 00:21:44,569
Don't move.

427
00:21:45,738 --> 00:21:46,762
Do you, uh...?

428
00:21:47,973 --> 00:21:49,965
Oh, yeah, I remember everything.

429
00:21:50,776 --> 00:21:51,869
Clear as day.

430
00:21:52,611 --> 00:21:53,655
And let me tell
you, if ever I see

431
00:21:53,679 --> 00:21:56,308
that Jervis Tetch character
again I'll stick that watch

432
00:21:56,448 --> 00:21:59,612
so far up his... his nose.

433
00:22:00,986 --> 00:22:02,045
How about you?

434
00:22:02,988 --> 00:22:04,320
You all right?

435
00:22:04,757 --> 00:22:06,089
Yeah, I'm all right.

436
00:22:07,526 --> 00:22:08,789
But the manor...

437
00:22:09,995 --> 00:22:11,964
Don't you worry
about that now, son.

438
00:22:12,731 --> 00:22:13,858
Come on. Help me up.

439
00:22:14,900 --> 00:22:16,630
(grunts, groans)

440
00:22:16,969 --> 00:22:17,969
Oh, your leg's hurt.

441
00:22:18,571 --> 00:22:20,096
Yes, but it's not broken.

442
00:22:25,845 --> 00:22:26,904
(grunts)

443
00:22:32,818 --> 00:22:34,377
I thought I lost you.

444
00:22:35,054 --> 00:22:36,054
Me?

445
00:22:37,690 --> 00:22:39,682
Never, Master Bruce.

446
00:22:42,628 --> 00:22:43,652
Go on.

447
00:22:44,930 --> 00:22:46,523
You know where he's gonna be at.

448
00:22:48,634 --> 00:22:49,634
Go.

449
00:23:01,981 --> 00:23:03,381
If you're here,

450
00:23:04,016 --> 00:23:06,042
Jeremiah must still be alive.

451
00:23:07,453 --> 00:23:10,048
And if you're here, I'm guessing
you found our test subjects,

452
00:23:10,389 --> 00:23:13,723
all boiled and
bubbled. (giggles)

453
00:23:13,993 --> 00:23:14,858
What's he planning?

454
00:23:14,994 --> 00:23:18,396
Shh. It's a surprise,
don't you know?

455
00:23:18,964 --> 00:23:21,024
A real killer.

456
00:23:21,767 --> 00:23:24,396
JERVIS: Shall I
hypnotize our friends here,

457
00:23:24,536 --> 00:23:25,981
and have them slit
each other's necks?

458
00:23:26,005 --> 00:23:27,598
ECCO: (laughs) Nix.

459
00:23:27,773 --> 00:23:29,503
Better check with the boss.

460
00:23:29,875 --> 00:23:32,401
He might have other ideas.

461
00:23:36,982 --> 00:23:38,712
I'm sorry I got you
involved in this.

462
00:23:39,118 --> 00:23:39,847
Don't be.

463
00:23:39,985 --> 00:23:41,396
I knew what I was
getting myself into.

464
00:23:41,420 --> 00:23:43,013
I know, but, Lee...

465
00:23:43,155 --> 00:23:45,818
Jim, whatever
you want to tell me,

466
00:23:45,991 --> 00:23:47,687
save it till we're out of here.

467
00:23:48,427 --> 00:23:49,427
Fair enough.

468
00:23:50,062 --> 00:23:52,463
We need to find out
what Valeska's planning.

469
00:23:53,465 --> 00:23:54,465
Hey, Tetch.

470
00:23:55,868 --> 00:23:57,200
You know, it's funny.

471
00:23:58,003 --> 00:24:00,871
I never figured you for
Jeremiah's errand boy.

472
00:24:01,206 --> 00:24:04,438
Oh, Captain. No
errands do I run.

473
00:24:04,610 --> 00:24:07,011
This is simply a way
for me to have some fun.

474
00:24:07,146 --> 00:24:09,581
THOMPKINS: (laughs)
Tell yourself that.

475
00:24:11,050 --> 00:24:12,814
What are you when
you would take away

476
00:24:12,952 --> 00:24:14,750
your games and your rhymes?

477
00:24:15,120 --> 00:24:17,612
Nothing but a second-rater
with a really silly hat.

478
00:24:18,524 --> 00:24:19,617
Shut up.

479
00:24:20,059 --> 00:24:21,925
(whispering)

480
00:24:22,161 --> 00:24:23,652
- (laughs)
- Beautiful.

481
00:24:23,796 --> 00:24:24,796
Beautiful.

482
00:24:26,165 --> 00:24:29,192
Lee Thompkins,
you do intrigue me so.

483
00:24:29,935 --> 00:24:32,131
First, you were a doctor,

484
00:24:33,038 --> 00:24:35,030
then the Narrows queen.

485
00:24:35,240 --> 00:24:36,708
Tell me, please do,

486
00:24:37,776 --> 00:24:39,870
are you running from your past

487
00:24:40,612 --> 00:24:42,547
when you become someone new?

488
00:24:52,224 --> 00:24:54,056
(door creaks)

489
00:25:05,971 --> 00:25:07,633
When I found Jeremiah,

490
00:25:07,940 --> 00:25:10,705
he had a bunch of crazies
digging this tunnel for him.

491
00:25:11,143 --> 00:25:13,806
Well, that certainly
fills me with confidence.

492
00:25:14,079 --> 00:25:17,607
- Whoa. You hear that?
- (rustling nearby)

493
00:25:18,784 --> 00:25:20,582
(footsteps approaching)

494
00:25:25,024 --> 00:25:26,720
- Alfred.
- Selina.

495
00:25:27,526 --> 00:25:28,687
What are you doing here?

496
00:25:29,795 --> 00:25:30,795
And with that?

497
00:25:31,530 --> 00:25:33,123
I should ask you the same thing.

498
00:25:33,265 --> 00:25:34,631
What's down that tunnel?

499
00:25:34,800 --> 00:25:36,928
Well, it was Wayne Manor
till Jeremiah blew it up.

500
00:25:38,037 --> 00:25:39,835
He sealed the only
way out of Gotham.

501
00:25:40,639 --> 00:25:41,639
SELINA: No.

502
00:25:41,707 --> 00:25:44,541
J-Jeremiah is not alive.
I-I saw him die right here.

503
00:25:44,676 --> 00:25:45,735
Yeah, well, you're wrong.

504
00:25:46,545 --> 00:25:47,638
We all were.

505
00:25:47,946 --> 00:25:50,313
And now he's embarked
on some madcap scheme

506
00:25:50,649 --> 00:25:52,961
where he's reenacting the
night Bruce's parents were killed.

507
00:25:52,985 --> 00:25:53,985
Where's Bruce?

508
00:25:54,119 --> 00:25:55,399
ALFRED: He's
gone after Jeremiah.

509
00:25:56,922 --> 00:25:58,117
He could use your help.

510
00:26:01,193 --> 00:26:01,922
Wait.

511
00:26:02,061 --> 00:26:04,189
Don't you think that because

512
00:26:04,329 --> 00:26:07,322
I did not kill Jeremiah does
not mean that I won't kill you.

513
00:26:07,800 --> 00:26:08,800
Selina.

514
00:26:08,867 --> 00:26:12,304
You killed my friend Tabitha.

515
00:26:13,572 --> 00:26:14,870
- You deserve to die.
- (grunts)

516
00:26:15,007 --> 00:26:16,031
Selina.

517
00:26:17,309 --> 00:26:19,005
Just put the knife down.

518
00:26:21,013 --> 00:26:22,641
Bruce needs you.

519
00:26:26,051 --> 00:26:28,748
(gasping)

520
00:26:38,964 --> 00:26:40,694
I suppose I should thank you.

521
00:26:41,300 --> 00:26:44,600
Or you could help
me to the Green Zone.

522
00:26:45,170 --> 00:26:47,765
Of course. It's that way.

523
00:27:04,389 --> 00:27:05,914
Jeremiah!

524
00:27:07,326 --> 00:27:08,988
Show yourself!

525
00:27:09,394 --> 00:27:11,329
(dramatic film score playing)

526
00:27:27,946 --> 00:27:29,847
♪♪

527
00:27:37,055 --> 00:27:38,055
Olé!

528
00:27:38,891 --> 00:27:40,325
Hola, Bruce.

529
00:27:40,792 --> 00:27:43,091
Well, here we are,

530
00:27:43,295 --> 00:27:46,732
the theater where your mommy
and daddy took you to see

531
00:27:46,965 --> 00:27:49,230
<i>The Mark of Zorro.</i>

532
00:27:50,269 --> 00:27:51,396
Ha-ha!

533
00:27:51,870 --> 00:27:54,339
I had heard you were
obsessed with this man as a child.

534
00:27:54,673 --> 00:27:57,074
I wonder what it was
that intrigued you so?

535
00:27:57,376 --> 00:27:59,106
Was it the fact
that he struck fear

536
00:27:59,244 --> 00:28:00,906
into the hearts of his enemy?

537
00:28:01,046 --> 00:28:03,345
♪♪

538
00:28:05,384 --> 00:28:06,443
En garde!

539
00:28:07,920 --> 00:28:08,683
Hee-yah!

540
00:28:08,820 --> 00:28:10,686
Take that, you villain.

541
00:28:11,323 --> 00:28:12,882
Vagabond.

542
00:28:14,326 --> 00:28:15,385
(screaming)

543
00:28:15,727 --> 00:28:17,923
- Scoundrel.
- (screaming)

544
00:28:18,130 --> 00:28:21,225
- (grunting)
- (laughing)
- (screaming)

545
00:28:21,366 --> 00:28:23,232
(dramatic music ends)

546
00:28:23,368 --> 00:28:24,927
Warned you.

547
00:28:25,804 --> 00:28:29,002
Perhaps the movie
was a bit too effective.

548
00:28:30,475 --> 00:28:33,775
Isn't this the part where
you became frightened?

549
00:28:33,912 --> 00:28:36,711
When you asked
your parents to leave?

550
00:28:37,382 --> 00:28:38,714
I wonder what
would have happened

551
00:28:38,850 --> 00:28:40,250
if you hadn't done that.

552
00:28:40,385 --> 00:28:43,287
If you had conquered your fear.

553
00:28:44,022 --> 00:28:47,117
Maybe your parents
would still be alive.

554
00:28:47,259 --> 00:28:49,160
♪♪

555
00:28:52,931 --> 00:28:55,196
Well, on to the last

556
00:28:55,334 --> 00:28:57,735
and final stop down memory lane.

557
00:28:57,869 --> 00:29:00,100
(filmstrip clicking)

558
00:29:04,943 --> 00:29:06,002
Stop!

559
00:29:07,212 --> 00:29:08,305
Stop!

560
00:29:08,447 --> 00:29:10,177
That's far enough, Bruce.

561
00:29:10,349 --> 00:29:11,442
BRUCE: Jeremiah.

562
00:29:12,451 --> 00:29:13,885
You don't have to do this.

563
00:29:14,019 --> 00:29:15,019
But I...

564
00:29:16,088 --> 00:29:17,088
I do.

565
00:29:18,156 --> 00:29:21,490
You see, I-I came
to this realization.

566
00:29:23,161 --> 00:29:25,392
I realized that no
matter what I did

567
00:29:25,530 --> 00:29:28,466
to bond us, some
random gunman in an alley

568
00:29:28,800 --> 00:29:31,531
would be the man who
you were tied to the most.

569
00:29:32,437 --> 00:29:35,464
The man you saw when
you closed your eyes.

570
00:29:36,808 --> 00:29:39,471
I want to be the
star of the show.

571
00:29:41,480 --> 00:29:45,315
So if I can't have you as
a brother bonded by love,

572
00:29:47,185 --> 00:29:49,984
then we'll just have to
be bonded by hatred.

573
00:29:50,289 --> 00:29:51,532
BRUCE: And you
think killing two people

574
00:29:51,556 --> 00:29:53,923
that look like my
parents will do that?

575
00:29:55,060 --> 00:29:55,925
It won't.

576
00:29:56,061 --> 00:29:57,438
Well, then it's a good
thing I already put

577
00:29:57,462 --> 00:30:01,024
a bullet in both of
their fraudulent skulls.

578
00:30:02,334 --> 00:30:03,927
Oh, you're confused.

579
00:30:04,069 --> 00:30:06,061
You're wondering if
I already shot them,

580
00:30:06,204 --> 00:30:09,572
then who's this lovely couple?

581
00:30:11,176 --> 00:30:13,008
Thomas, Martha...

582
00:30:14,246 --> 00:30:16,215
why don't you turn around?

583
00:30:30,595 --> 00:30:32,996
- Jim!
- (Jeremiah laughs)

584
00:30:33,131 --> 00:30:34,258
I know.

585
00:30:34,566 --> 00:30:37,832
See, o-over the course
of our little adventure,

586
00:30:37,969 --> 00:30:42,031
fate brought to me James
Gordon and Leslie Thompkins,

587
00:30:42,174 --> 00:30:46,839
and I thought to
myself, why not...

588
00:30:48,213 --> 00:30:50,409
why not kill the
man who you think of

589
00:30:50,549 --> 00:30:52,575
as your second father figure?

590
00:30:53,218 --> 00:30:55,551
And your dear, dear,

591
00:30:55,887 --> 00:30:59,153
dear friend Lee Thompkins.

592
00:31:00,125 --> 00:31:01,388
And when I do,

593
00:31:02,160 --> 00:31:04,925
finally, you and I will
be bound together.

594
00:31:05,130 --> 00:31:06,130
Because you see...

595
00:31:06,298 --> 00:31:08,858
("La Cucaracha" plays)

596
00:31:12,304 --> 00:31:16,173
re-unification with the
mainland hangs on by a thread.

597
00:31:16,375 --> 00:31:17,934
Those fireworks go off

598
00:31:18,210 --> 00:31:20,907
and toxic chemicals
rain down onto the city,

599
00:31:21,046 --> 00:31:23,106
and the government...
(clicks tongue)

600
00:31:23,248 --> 00:31:25,114
cuts us adrift for good.

601
00:31:31,523 --> 00:31:32,523
BRUCE: Jeremiah.

602
00:31:34,126 --> 00:31:35,126
Don't.

603
00:31:35,260 --> 00:31:36,260
Shh.

604
00:31:36,928 --> 00:31:39,056
The pièce de résistance.

605
00:31:39,664 --> 00:31:41,257
One last thing.

606
00:31:41,600 --> 00:31:43,967
I had Jervis Tetch
hypnotize them

607
00:31:44,102 --> 00:31:45,434
so that they'll wake
up the moment

608
00:31:45,570 --> 00:31:49,337
these beautiful
pearls hit the ground.

609
00:31:50,442 --> 00:31:53,105
I want you to see them
realize what I've done to them

610
00:31:53,245 --> 00:31:56,306
as the life drains
from their bodies.

611
00:31:57,382 --> 00:31:58,645
Never forget,

612
00:31:59,418 --> 00:32:01,546
this is all for you, Bruce.

613
00:32:02,287 --> 00:32:03,287
No!

614
00:32:10,529 --> 00:32:12,054
Selina! The pearls!

615
00:32:24,209 --> 00:32:26,371
Ecco! Now!

616
00:32:27,612 --> 00:32:31,413
(timer beeping)

617
00:32:34,653 --> 00:32:35,853
We need to stop the fireworks.

618
00:32:35,954 --> 00:32:37,034
- They're gonna...
- I know.

619
00:32:37,255 --> 00:32:39,383
You go after Jeremiah
and Ecco. I'll take the truck!

620
00:32:44,196 --> 00:32:45,562
There's no way to stop them all.

621
00:32:46,398 --> 00:32:47,661
Get to Harvey.

622
00:32:48,633 --> 00:32:51,330
Warn the people in the
Green Zone to get to cover.

623
00:32:51,636 --> 00:32:54,572
What are you... Jim!

624
00:33:03,181 --> 00:33:04,479
Jeremiah!

625
00:33:05,183 --> 00:33:06,207
Face me!

626
00:33:07,118 --> 00:33:08,245
Here, Bruce.

627
00:33:34,312 --> 00:33:35,610
(beeping rapidly)

628
00:33:49,728 --> 00:33:51,253
Jeremiah!

629
00:33:52,764 --> 00:33:54,062
This ends.

630
00:33:54,799 --> 00:33:57,701
- Tonight.
- No.

631
00:33:58,336 --> 00:34:00,362
No, Bruce. Now it begins.

632
00:34:00,505 --> 00:34:01,529
(laughs)

633
00:34:16,688 --> 00:34:17,688
(groans)

634
00:34:18,123 --> 00:34:19,352
Yes.

635
00:34:20,158 --> 00:34:23,322
You feel it. The
connection between us.

636
00:34:24,195 --> 00:34:25,219
You do.

637
00:34:25,397 --> 00:34:28,196
Don't you? Bruce, you feel it.

638
00:34:29,100 --> 00:34:30,261
Tell me you feel it.

639
00:34:30,502 --> 00:34:31,663
(groans)

640
00:34:33,738 --> 00:34:35,764
You mean nothing to me.

641
00:34:40,679 --> 00:34:42,841
Why don't you understand?

642
00:34:45,750 --> 00:34:47,378
You need me.

643
00:34:48,286 --> 00:34:50,755
I'm the answer to
your life's question!

644
00:34:51,656 --> 00:34:54,285
Without me,
you're just a joke...

645
00:34:57,262 --> 00:34:59,288
without a punch line.

646
00:35:26,825 --> 00:35:28,726
♪♪

647
00:36:00,325 --> 00:36:01,793
After all this time,

648
00:36:02,560 --> 00:36:05,496
you've come to me for help.

649
00:36:06,364 --> 00:36:09,528
After allowing Strange
to put a chip into my brain.

650
00:36:09,668 --> 00:36:11,534
Attempting to sell
me out to Gordon.

651
00:36:12,170 --> 00:36:13,365
And after naming...

652
00:36:15,440 --> 00:36:17,341
a dog after me.

653
00:36:17,676 --> 00:36:18,735
First of all,

654
00:36:19,577 --> 00:36:22,411
I am very fond of that dog.

655
00:36:22,580 --> 00:36:27,450
Secondly, I had Hugo
Strange save your life.

656
00:36:27,619 --> 00:36:29,850
Thirdly, do you really think

657
00:36:30,188 --> 00:36:30,848
I didn't have plans

658
00:36:31,189 --> 00:36:34,250
to save you from Jim Gordon?

659
00:36:34,392 --> 00:36:36,418
(chuckles)

660
00:36:37,228 --> 00:36:39,588
You always have an answer
for everything, don't you, Oswald?

661
00:36:40,365 --> 00:36:43,927
We have been through
all of this before.

662
00:36:44,269 --> 00:36:45,669
I've tried to kill you.

663
00:36:46,404 --> 00:36:47,929
You've tried to kill me.

664
00:36:48,807 --> 00:36:51,470
But here we are in this room.

665
00:36:51,776 --> 00:36:52,776
Together.

666
00:36:55,313 --> 00:36:57,612
It means fate has
different plans for us.

667
00:37:02,854 --> 00:37:04,288
What are these plans?

668
00:37:05,323 --> 00:37:07,451
Haven't you realized
what Gotham is yet?

669
00:37:08,393 --> 00:37:10,294
It is no longer a city.

670
00:37:10,995 --> 00:37:12,520
It is a prison.

671
00:37:14,365 --> 00:37:16,334
And I think it's
time we escaped.

672
00:37:31,516 --> 00:37:32,745
You heard the news?

673
00:37:32,984 --> 00:37:34,475
Everybody's talking about it.

674
00:37:35,253 --> 00:37:36,846
Reunification isn't happening.

675
00:37:37,322 --> 00:37:39,348
Word of the chemical
spill reached the mainland.

676
00:37:39,791 --> 00:37:43,284
No action until the government
can determine if Gotham is safe.

677
00:37:43,695 --> 00:37:45,630
I figure at least a
couple of months.

678
00:37:46,865 --> 00:37:48,424
You don't sound surprised.

679
00:37:49,367 --> 00:37:50,528
Guess I'm not.

680
00:37:52,370 --> 00:37:53,736
Could've been much worse.

681
00:37:54,305 --> 00:37:56,297
- You stopped that.
- (sighs)

682
00:37:56,541 --> 00:37:58,285
Every time I think we're
turning things around,

683
00:37:58,309 --> 00:38:00,744
I look up... Right
back where we started.

684
00:38:12,323 --> 00:38:13,757
What were you about to say to me

685
00:38:14,359 --> 00:38:16,055
when, uh, Tetch had us?

686
00:38:21,866 --> 00:38:23,027
I don't know.

687
00:38:23,968 --> 00:38:27,302
I guess I, uh,
would have said...

688
00:38:28,606 --> 00:38:30,837
what I said the last
time we saw each other.

689
00:38:34,712 --> 00:38:36,578
I wish I could go back.

690
00:38:38,449 --> 00:38:39,815
Do things differently.

691
00:38:40,752 --> 00:38:41,752
Better.

692
00:38:46,024 --> 00:38:49,324
- It feels like a long time ago.
- Nothing's changed.

693
00:38:50,395 --> 00:38:51,863
But it has, Jim.

694
00:38:54,365 --> 00:38:54,957
That was a mistake.

695
00:38:55,099 --> 00:38:56,362
A mistake?

696
00:38:56,901 --> 00:38:59,871
Put yourself in my shoes.
After everything you said,

697
00:39:00,004 --> 00:39:03,406
suddenly you're having a
baby with Barbara, of all people.

698
00:39:07,345 --> 00:39:08,677
But it's not just that.

699
00:39:09,914 --> 00:39:11,425
You talk about doing
things differently

700
00:39:11,449 --> 00:39:12,747
and I keep thinking,

701
00:39:14,752 --> 00:39:16,687
what if we hadn't lost ours?

702
00:39:24,629 --> 00:39:26,120
What are you doing here, Lee?

703
00:39:29,767 --> 00:39:30,860
I don't know.

704
00:39:32,470 --> 00:39:34,837
I know you've taken
on so much, and...

705
00:39:36,374 --> 00:39:38,366
and I want to be
understanding, but...

706
00:39:40,044 --> 00:39:41,672
you let me down, Jim.

707
00:39:45,383 --> 00:39:46,544
I'm sorry.

708
00:39:51,522 --> 00:39:53,787
- What does that mean?
- (sighs)

709
00:39:54,125 --> 00:39:55,388
For us?

710
00:39:55,960 --> 00:39:56,984
I don't know.

711
00:39:58,930 --> 00:39:59,954
Can't change the past,

712
00:40:00,098 --> 00:40:02,761
so I guess we just
have to live with it.

713
00:40:06,404 --> 00:40:07,667
No, Lee...

714
00:40:24,989 --> 00:40:26,890
(monitor beeping steadily)

715
00:40:29,794 --> 00:40:33,458
SELINA: I can't
believe he's still alive.

716
00:40:34,432 --> 00:40:37,425
They've been doing scans,
and he has no brain activity.

717
00:40:38,536 --> 00:40:40,129
He's no longer a threat.

718
00:40:42,807 --> 00:40:44,469
To either of us.

719
00:40:51,516 --> 00:40:53,610
Thank you for coming to help me.

720
00:40:57,221 --> 00:40:58,621
That night your
parents were killed,

721
00:40:58,656 --> 00:41:00,682
I should have done something.

722
00:41:02,694 --> 00:41:04,492
Selina, you've done enough.

723
00:41:11,836 --> 00:41:14,738
(thunder rumbles)

724
00:41:16,007 --> 00:41:17,839
It's not much, but it's home.

725
00:41:17,976 --> 00:41:20,002
I've been looking through
your treasure trove.

726
00:41:20,678 --> 00:41:23,477
- You've been a very naughty boy.
- Barbara?

727
00:41:23,648 --> 00:41:24,911
How did you...

728
00:41:26,651 --> 00:41:27,651
Selina?

729
00:41:27,919 --> 00:41:31,686
Hmm. She and I were
gonna go murder-halfsies

730
00:41:31,823 --> 00:41:33,553
to get you back for Tabitha,

731
00:41:33,758 --> 00:41:36,250
but it seems I will have
to do the dirty work myself,

732
00:41:36,594 --> 00:41:37,687
as usual.

733
00:41:37,829 --> 00:41:38,922
NYGMA: Oh, my God.

734
00:41:41,199 --> 00:41:42,599
You're pregnant.

735
00:41:45,003 --> 00:41:47,700
- How could you
possibly know that?
- Look at you.

736
00:41:48,039 --> 00:41:49,098
She's glowing.

737
00:41:49,807 --> 00:41:51,105
You're glowing.

738
00:41:51,743 --> 00:41:54,235
How very observant
of you. Adieu, Oswald.

739
00:41:54,612 --> 00:41:55,636
Wait!

740
00:41:56,214 --> 00:41:57,614
Come with us.

741
00:41:58,916 --> 00:42:00,782
- What?
- Yes.

742
00:42:01,686 --> 00:42:03,917
I killed Tabitha.

743
00:42:04,555 --> 00:42:05,579
You're angry.

744
00:42:05,857 --> 00:42:08,588
You want revenge.
But do you really want

745
00:42:08,726 --> 00:42:12,857
to raise your child in a
toxic waste war zone?

746
00:42:14,098 --> 00:42:15,760
Come with us.

747
00:42:17,301 --> 00:42:19,793
Are you telling me you
found a way out of Gotham?

748
00:42:20,271 --> 00:42:21,271
Ed did.

749
00:42:24,175 --> 00:42:25,268
It's a submarine.

750
00:42:26,010 --> 00:42:27,205
- A submarine?
- It can track

751
00:42:27,545 --> 00:42:29,639
mines in the river using sonar.

752
00:42:32,817 --> 00:42:34,046
So, where's this submarine?

753
00:42:39,924 --> 00:42:40,983
We have to build it.

754
00:42:41,225 --> 00:42:42,825
- Yeah, I'm gonna shoot you.
- (whimpers)

755
00:42:45,296 --> 00:42:46,296
God.

756
00:42:47,732 --> 00:42:48,859
What is happening to me?

757
00:42:49,734 --> 00:42:51,134
- Perhaps...
- Shut up!

758
00:42:51,269 --> 00:42:53,101
That was a rhetorical question.

759
00:42:55,239 --> 00:42:56,571
(sighs)

760
00:42:57,675 --> 00:42:58,904
Fine.

761
00:42:59,644 --> 00:43:02,307
I won't shoot you for
the sake of my child.

762
00:43:03,214 --> 00:43:06,343
- But I will never forgive you.
- Of course.

763
00:43:07,351 --> 00:43:08,979
I understand.

764
00:43:13,758 --> 00:43:14,919
Call me when it's done.

765
00:43:15,059 --> 00:43:17,290
- So, who's the lucky father?
- Shut up!
